meta {
  name: ListAccounts
  type: grpc
  seq: 2
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.IdentityService/ListAccounts
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "user": { "id": "u-1" }
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  Every RPC of the domain carries a `CallContext` — who, in which account. The
  edge fills it in; the domain trusts it (ADR-0016).
}
